  "source": "Goldman Sachs",
  "title": "H World Group (HTHT): Asia Leaders Conference 2026 Takeaways: New signings and hotel adds on track. Supply chain the key focus but hard to",
  "type": "equity_research",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-09-03",
  "insights": [
   "H World management reports resilient leisure demand but sluggish business travel, with B2B corporate customers accounting for low-teens percentage of total room nights.",
   "Mature hotels face intense competition from new supply, resulting in same-hotel RevPar -3% yoy in 2Q26.",
   "Management is rationalizing regional pricing strategies to minimize cannibalization between new and mature hotels, expanding this initiative from Shanghai to broader Eastern China.",
   "New signing momentum remains stable at ~2.8-2.9k annually, with the company continuing to gain market share despite franchisee caution.",
   "Full-year gross opening target of 2.2-2.3k hotels remains intact, with momentum picking up in July-August after a slow 1H26.",
   "Hotel closures are expected to remain at 600-700 per annum as the company phases out older products like Hanting 3.5.",
   "Payback periods for new signings are strictly controlled at 3-5 years, supported by pricing premiums, direct booking volume (60-65%), and supply chain efficiencies.",
   "The company is leveraging its 14.3k hotel network and Rmb100bn hotel GMV to negotiate lower procurement costs, though it does not provide specific guidance on supply chain revenue upside.",
   "Asset-light overseas expansion into Southeast Asia is progressing, with a new division (HWI) formalized in 1Q26 to target a few hotel additions per annum."
  ],
